<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.7.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00959</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.7.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>373b4475-d054-4dbb-99ba-51e2c091b041</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> Evaluate \(\frac{140-20}{9-12}\) mentally. </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> -40</para>
<para>\(\frac{140-20}{9-12}=\frac{120}{-3}=-40\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> Find the slope of the line that goes through the points \((1,-3)\) and \((2,4)\).:</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 7</para>
<para>\(m=\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}=\frac{4-(-3)}{2-1}=\frac{7}{1}=7\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item> Write the equation of the line in slope-intercept form that goes through \((0,3)\) and has a slope of \(\frac14\) .</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(y = -\frac{1}{4}x + 3\) </item>
  <item>\(
    y = \frac{1}{4}x + 3\) </item>
  <item>\(
    y = 3x + \frac{1}{4}\) </item>
  <item>\(
    4x - y = -3 \)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(y = \frac{1}{4}x + 3\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item> Write the equation of the line that passes through \((2,-1)\) and has a slope of \(-\frac{1}{2}\) in point-slope form.</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\(
    y = -\frac{1}{2}x -1 \)</item>
  <item>\(
    y +1 = -\frac{1}{2}(x - 2) \)</item>
  <item>\(
    y = -\frac{1}{2}x \)</item>
  <item>\(
    2x + y = 0 \)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(y+1 = - \frac{1}{2}(x - 2)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item><emphasis> Select two</emphasis> equations that are correctly in standard form.</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(6x - 3y = 3 \)</item>
  <item>\(
    -4x + 5y = 9 \)</item>
  <item>\(
    \frac{1}{2}x + 3y = 8 \)</item>
  <item>\(
    5x + 2y = 9\) </item>
  <item>\(
    5y + 2x = 10 \)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(6x - 3y = 3\) and \(5x + 2y = 9\)</para>
<para>\(6x - 3y = 3\) and \(5x + 2y = 9\) are in standard form because they are of the form \(Ax + By = C\).</para>
<para>They do not have any fractions or decimals and start with a positive coefficient.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item> Write \(y = 4x - 2\) in standard form. </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(4x -y = 2\)</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y &amp;=&amp; 4x - 2\\ y - 4x &amp;=&amp; 4x - 4x - 2\\ -4x + y &amp;=&amp; -2 \\-1(-4x + y &amp;=&amp; -2) \\4x - y &amp;=&amp; 2\end{array}\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item> Write the equation \(y-4=-2(x-5)\) in slope-intercept form. </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(y=-2x+14\)</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y-4&amp;=&amp;-2(x-5) \\ y-4&amp;=&amp;-2x+10\\ y&amp;=&amp;-2x+10+4\\ y&amp;=&amp;-2x+14\end{array}\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item> Find the slope of the line between the points \((3,-1)\) and \((2,-4)\). </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 3</para>
<para>\(m=\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}=\frac{-4-(-1)}{2-3}=\frac{-3}{-1}=3\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <item> Write the equation \(y-2=3(x+5)\) in standard form. </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(3x-y=-17\)</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y-2&amp;=&amp;3(x+5)\\y-2&amp;=&amp;3x+15\\y-2-3x&amp;=&amp;3x-3x+15\\y-3x-2&amp;=&amp;15\\y-3x&amp;=&amp;15+2\\y-3x&amp;=&amp;17\\-1-(3x+y&amp;=&amp;17)\\3x-y&amp;=&amp;-17\end{array}\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
  <item> Evaluate \(\frac{36-48}{10-14}\) mentally. </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 3</para>
<para>\(\frac{36-48}{10-14} =\frac{-12}{-4}=3\)</para>
</section>
